        # ReleaseNotes of this module
        ReleaseNotes = 'v2.5.1 -- Seven fixes that let a full inventory run complete against a real tenant. Every one was found by running the product end to end against live Azure; the 1692-test suite passed throughout because nothing drove the extraction, processing and reporting chain against real collector output. Extraction: $MGContainerExtension was consumed unconditionally by the resourcecontainers query but only assigned in the -ManagementGroup branch, so a run without that switch died on an unset variable (AB#5547). Processing: 41 .IsPresent reads on parameters not declared [switch] -- $null when the caller omits them -- replaced with a null-safe [bool] coercion (AB#5547). Reporting (AB#5567): ImportExcel throws on a -Style range or -TableName over a worksheet with zero data rows, so both are now supplied only when there is at least one row; the cost and update-manager worksheets read $vm.Name/$vm.Size/OS SKU against a collector that emits VM Name/VM Size/OS Version, so those sheets had never carried VM rows; 29 worksheet dereferences threw whenever the estate produced no such sheet (no public IPs, no disks, no VMs) and now resolve through a Worksheets lookup; 10 pivot titles were read before assignment; and the Markdown export died on a trailing italic underscore parsed as part of the identifier. Verified live: 227 Azure resources, 994 Excel rows, 40 Power BI CSVs, plus JSON, Markdown and the draw.io diagram, with Azure DevOps extraction returning 166 resources across 74 projects -- the first live-tenant verification of the -IncludeDevOps collectors. Known limitation: Build-AZSCExcelComObject emits a non-fatal error when Excel is not installed; the run completes regardless. Full suite 1692 passed, 0 failed, 3 skipped. v2.5.0 -- One collection pass. A combined inventory + assessment run now queries Azure once instead of twice (AB#5543). The inventory pass already projects the full properties bag from resources, networkresources and resourcecontainers, a superset of what the assessment typed queries were re-fetching, so the assessment shapes its scalars from those in-memory rows via ConvertFrom-ScoutInventory instead of issuing its own Resource Graph pack. Exactly one query still reaches Resource Graph in a combined run: sqlDefenderPricing reads the SecurityResources table, which inventory only touches under -SecurityCenter. The assessment-only path is unchanged and the KQL remains the reference implementation. v2.4.0 -- One command, and a guided wizard. Inventory and assessment are modes of a single Invoke-AzureScout rather than two cmdlets: Invoke-AzureScout -Assessment runs the CAF/WAF assessment, and without -Assessment the command behaves as before. -CollectOnly and -FromCollect moved onto Invoke-AzureScout, and assessment mode now honours the inventory sign-in parameters. -OutputFormat widened to [string[]] so one run can request several renderers. DEPRECATED: Invoke-ScoutAssessment still works but will be removed in v3.0.0. NEW: running Invoke-AzureScout with no parameters in an interactive session opens a guided wizard; it never fires in a non-interactive host, and -NoWizard forces that path. Full history for every earlier release is in CHANGELOG.md: https://github.com/thisismydemo/azure-scout/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md'

        # Prerelease string of this module
        # Prerelease = ''

